    "itemBodyHtml": "<div class=\"row\">\n\t<div class=\"span6\"><div class=\"passageContent\" xml:base=\"VF581304_s.xml\"><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"passage-intro\">Today you will read two articles about advances in weather forecasting.</p></div></div>\n    \t<div class=\"stimulus\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"passage-scrolling passage440\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"passageContent\" xml:base=\"VF582182.xml\"><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"directions-passage\" id=\"sr58\">Read the article “At Your Fingertips.” Then answer the questions.</p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"passage-title\">At Your Fingertips</p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"author center\"><em>by</em> Ruth Tenzer Feldman</p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p><span class=\"badge badge-inverse\">1</span> You can find all kinds of weather information, from today’s clouds over Topeka to next year’s predicted rainfall on the West Coast, by going to the National Weather Service (NWS) at www.weather.gov.</p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p><span class=\"badge badge-inverse\">2</span> The NWS is the federal agency that provides weather, hydrologic (water-related), and climate forecasts and warnings for the nation, including U.S. territories and ocean areas. The agency, an arm of the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA), has about 4,800 employees in 131 weather forecast offices, 19 river forecast centers, and 6 national centers. The NWS has teams of scientists studying satellite, buoy, radar, and computer information to forecast when and where any given condition will likely occur.</p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p><span class=\"badge badge-inverse\">3</span> The NWS Storm Prediction Center forecasts severe weather up to three days in advance and updates information as severe weather approaches. A weather alert system now warns people about 11 minutes before a tornado strikes—which is about 11 minutes longer than people had 20 years ago!</p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p><span class=\"badge badge-inverse\">4</span> The Climate Prediction Center studies weather patterns lasting months or years. These depend on the El Niño-Southern Oscillation (ENSO), which is a measure of the surface temperature of the tropical Pacific Ocean. Every month, the center publishes the ENSO Diagnostic Discussion forecasting climate conditions in the nation.</p></div><div class=\"abbi-image\"><p class=\"center\"><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/previewer-prd-tn8-resources/items/1040/680dc174-2cec-443c-a430-710eac066e76/assets/VF582182.g02.png\" alt=\" \" width=\"385\" height=\"363\"/></p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p><span class=\"badge badge-inverse\">5</span> NWS information is used for adjusting airline flight routes, protecting property from floods or hurricanes, managing crop harvests, and even stocking up on toilet paper.</p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p><span class=\"badge badge-inverse\">6</span> Each year, Americans get more than 1,584,000 NWS forecasts as well as up to 50,000 potentially life-saving severe weather warnings. So the next time the NWS accurately predicts a clap of thunder—or anything else—be sure to give the agency some appreciative claps of your own.</p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p> </p> <p class=\"copyright-tm\">“At Your Fingertips” by Ruth Tenzer Feldman from COBBLESTONE, Carus Publishing Co. © 2012.</p></div></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"span6\"><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><h4>Part A</h4></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"stem_paragraph\" id=\"c2\">Which idea in “At Your Fingertips” is <b class=\"stressed_text_1\">best </b>illustrated by the graphic in the article?</p></div>\n\n<ul class=\"int-choice-list choice_list \" data-module=\"ChoiceInteraction\" data-maxchoices=\"1\" data-minchoices=\"1\" data-identifier=\"interaction_RESPONSE_A\">\n<li>\n\t<label class=\"radio\" for=\"choice_526b2\">\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-control choicerAi1\">\n\t\t\t<input type=\"radio\" id=\"choice_526b2\" name=\"group_RESPONSE_A\" value=\"rAi1\" />\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-label\">\n\t\t\tA.\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div  class=\"int-choice-desc \"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"c3\">The NWS is a large organization.</p></div>\n\t</label>\n</li>\n<li>\n\t<label class=\"radio\" for=\"choice_289b2\">\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-control choicerAi2\">\n\t\t\t<input type=\"radio\" id=\"choice_289b2\" name=\"group_RESPONSE_A\" value=\"rAi2\" />\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-label\">\n\t\t\tB.\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div  class=\"int-choice-desc \"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"c4\">The NWS helps save many lives every year.</p></div>\n\t</label>\n</li>\n<li>\n\t<label class=\"radio\" for=\"choice_672bb\">\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-control choicerAi3\">\n\t\t\t<input type=\"radio\" id=\"choice_672bb\" name=\"group_RESPONSE_A\" value=\"rAi3\" />\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-label\">\n\t\t\tC.\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div  class=\"int-choice-desc \"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"c5\">The NWS provides the weather for the country.</p></div>\n\t</label>\n</li>\n<li>\n\t<label class=\"radio\" for=\"choice_80d41\">\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-control choicerAi4\">\n\t\t\t<input type=\"radio\" id=\"choice_80d41\" name=\"group_RESPONSE_A\" value=\"rAi4\" />\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-label\">\n\t\t\tD.\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div  class=\"int-choice-desc \"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"c6\">The NWS has different ways to determine the weather.</p></div>\n\t</label>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p></p></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><h4>Part B</h4></div><div class=\"abbi-richtext\"><p class=\"stem_paragraph\" id=\"c8\">Which detail from paragraph 2 of the article <b class=\"stressed_text_1\">best </b>supports the answer to Part A?</p></div>\n\n<ul class=\"int-choice-list choice_list \" data-module=\"ChoiceInteraction\" data-maxchoices=\"1\" data-minchoices=\"1\" data-identifier=\"interaction_RESPONSE_B\">\n<li>\n\t<label class=\"radio\" for=\"choice_0f402\">\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-control choicerBi1\">\n\t\t\t<input type=\"radio\" id=\"choice_0f402\" name=\"group_RESPONSE_B\" value=\"rBi1\" />\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-label\">\n\t\t\tA.\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div  class=\"int-choice-desc \"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"c9\">“. . . the federal agency . . .”</p></div>\n\t</label>\n</li>\n<li>\n\t<label class=\"radio\" for=\"choice_32270\">\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-control choicerBi2\">\n\t\t\t<input type=\"radio\" id=\"choice_32270\" name=\"group_RESPONSE_B\" value=\"rBi2\" />\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-label\">\n\t\t\tB.\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div  class=\"int-choice-desc \"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"c10\">“. . . warnings for the nation . . .”</p></div>\n\t</label>\n</li>\n<li>\n\t<label class=\"radio\" for=\"choice_31dff\">\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-control choicerBi3\">\n\t\t\t<input type=\"radio\" id=\"choice_31dff\" name=\"group_RESPONSE_B\" value=\"rBi3\" />\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-label\">\n\t\t\tC.\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div  class=\"int-choice-desc \"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"c11\">“. . . ocean areas.”</p></div>\n\t</label>\n</li>\n<li>\n\t<label class=\"radio\" for=\"choice_9cb62\">\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-control choicerBi4\">\n\t\t\t<input type=\"radio\" id=\"choice_9cb62\" name=\"group_RESPONSE_B\" value=\"rBi4\" />\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div class=\"int-choice-label\">\n\t\t\tD.\n\t\t</div>\n\t\t<div  class=\"int-choice-desc \"><p class=\"choice_paragraph\" id=\"c12\">“. . . computer information . . .”</p></div>\n\t</label>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n",
